mypy note: google-cloud-spanner and google-api-core ship py.typed but leave
public functions unannotated, so strict mode read normal calls as untyped ones.
ignore_missing_imports cannot fix that — the modules are found, just
under-typed — so untyped_calls_exclude names the two packages instead. That is
narrower than relaxing disallow_untyped_calls for our own modules.

